        "date_published": "2026-09-22T14:00:10+00:00",
        "description": "The White House has launched an online television channel called \u2018Trump TV\u2019, hours after major television networks in the US suspended their pooled coverage in protest of CNN, Politico and MS NOW being barred from the White House.\n \nTrump TV operates a 24/7 feed of clips of the president. Initial coverage included Trump taking part in a ribbon-cutting ceremony for the new Marine One helipad on the White House South Lawn, but his comments were inaudible.\n \nThe three media organisations banned from the White House filed a lawsuit on Monday in US District Court in Washington.\n \nSubscribe to our channel here: https://bbc.in/bbcnews\n \nFor the latest news download the BBC News app or visit BBC.com/news\n \n#Trump #USPolitics #BBCNews",
